# Derp: charger-token-boot handoff.
#
# From system/core/init/init.cpp:
#
#     std::string bootmode = GetProperty("ro.bootmode", "");
#     if (bootmode == "charger") {
#         am.QueueEventTrigger("charger");     // class_start charger
#     } else {
#         am.QueueEventTrigger("late-init");   // normal boot proceeds
#     }
#
# So on a charger-token boot init deliberately queues "charger" and never
# queues "late-init". healthd takes the display and the rest of Android -
# zygote, system_server - never starts, so the phone sits on the charging
# animation indefinitely. The only escape is init.rc's
#
#     on property:sys.boot_from_charger_mode=1
#         class_stop charger
#         trigger late-init
#
# and that property is set in exactly one place: healthd_mode_charger.cpp,
# after a 2 s power-key hold (POWER_ON_KEY_TIME = 2 * MSEC_PER_SEC). With
# ro.charger_mode_autoboot unset nothing hands off on its own, which is why
# only a long press - a "hard reset" - ever got past it.
#
# This performs that handoff directly. Both are init builtins, so there is no
# property_service check and no SELinux domain involved - deliberately, after
# a first attempt that used "setprop sys.boot_from_charger_mode 1" and booted
# into a loop (init re-ran late-init, which re-ran post-fs-data, which set the
# property again). Doing this from a property trigger removes that possibility:
# the trigger fires once, when ro.bootmode becomes charger, and late-init
# would otherwise never have run at all on this boot.
#
# The co-processors used to stay dead on a charger-token boot even after this
# handoff - the CP reset sequencer stuck at RESET_SEQUENCER_STATUS 0x3 instead
# of 0x5, the mx140 WLAN firmware never answered, so there was no WiFi and no
# RIL - and a one-shot warm reboot guarded around it. That is fixed at the root
# in the kernel instead: s2mpu08_pmic_probe() cleared the enable bits on
# LDO16/LDO17/LDO15/Buck9 whenever lpcharge was set, i.e. on every
# charger-token boot, and keeping them up takes the CP to 0x5 with 0 pmucal
# timeouts and a live baseband (verified 5/5 consecutive charger boots). The
# reboot guard and its script are therefore removed; they also exec'd
# u:r:su:s0, which does not exist here (root is u:r:ksu:s0), so they never ran.

on property:ro.bootmode=charger
    class_stop charger
    trigger late-init
